      "name": "spectrafit-core reps-ladder benchmark — ladder-20260815T184025Z",
      "description": "Cross-backend curve-fitting benchmark run at a ladder of repetition depths, with per-rung provenance. Records the geometric-mean speedup of spectrafit-core against lmfit, jax/optimistix and three scipy.optimize.least_squares methods over a deterministic 151-case catalogue, together with the solver configuration, timing methodology, accuracy definitions and machine environment needed to interpret or recompute those numbers. Every rung ran on one host in one process; see ladder.json for the methodology block and the comparability caveats. The per-rung result payloads (results.json.gz, audit.json.gz, run.log) are large and are not duplicated into this directory; they stay with the run that produced them and are not distributed here. This crate describes only what is present here, so its checksums verify.",
